[h1]REPO Command Console: spawn items, revive players, and run your first commands[/h1]

This tutorial covers [b]RepoCommandConsole 2.1.0[/b] for R.E.P.O. Start with one item, learn autocomplete, then try the player commands. The mod uses a separate F2 console with host-controlled multiplayer permissions.

[url=https://thunderstore.io/c/repo/p/Coollectors/RepoCommandConsole/]Install RepoCommandConsole[/url] · [url=https://github.com/jkieley/repo-live-control/blob/main/docs/commands.md]Complete command reference[/url]

[h2]1. Install with Thunderstore or r2modman[/h2]

1. Open Thunderstore Mod Manager or r2modman and select [b]R.E.P.O.[/b]
2. Create or choose a profile. Search for [b]RepoCommandConsole by Coollectors[/b] and download it.
3. Confirm that [b]BepInExPack 5.4.2305[/b] and [b]REPOLib 4.2.0[/b] are installed as dependencies.
4. Choose [b]Start Modded[/b], then enter a lobby or run.
5. Press [b]F2[/b] to open the console.

This version targets R.E.P.O. [b]v0.4.4.3[/b]. For multiplayer, the host and everyone who wants to submit commands need the mod. Use 2.1.0 or newer for the player commands in this guide. AllPlayerCommands is not required.

[h2]2. Find an item without memorizing its internal name[/h2]

Type /spawn, use [b]Up/Down[/b] to highlight the command, and press [b]Tab[/b]. Type strength, then select the live [b]Strength Upgrade[/b] item suggestion and press [b]Tab[/b] again. Autocomplete supplies the catalog prefix and quotes. Press [b]Enter[/b] to execute.

The accepted command typically looks like:

[code]/spawn "item:Strength Upgrade"
[/code]

The default count is one, and the default location is the player who submitted the command. Read the result before submitting another command. Press [b]Escape[/b] or [b]F2[/b] to close the console and inspect the item.

[url=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jkieley/repo-live-control/166dbec2d6298abb351ef05fc1f8dfb250fb2e12/docs/promotion/screenshots/repo-command-console-autocomplete.jpg]See the actual autocomplete interface[/url]. This screenshot was captured with version 2.0.0; other installed mods provide some surrounding HUD.

Fuzzy search helps you find names; execution uses the exact suggestion you accepted. When an example name is absent, select an available entry from your current game instead.

[h2]3. Spawn equipment, valuables, or an enemy[/h2]

Targets come from three catalogs: item: for equipment, weapons and upgrades; valuable: for loot; and enemy: for enemies.

[code]/spawn "item:Strength Upgrade" 2 player-location
/spawn "valuable:Diamond Display" 3 random-non-collision-location
/spawn "enemy:Headman" 1 random-non-collision-location
[/code]

Use autocomplete to confirm the target before running each example. random-non-collision-location searches the level for a clear position, so the result may be outside your view. Counts must be whole numbers from [b]1 through 500[/b]. If placement fails, the console reports the problem; use a smaller count or try another location.

[h2]4. Clean up what you spawned[/h2]

[code]/despawn "item:Strength Upgrade" all
/despawn "valuable:Diamond Display" all
/despawn "enemy:Headman" all
[/code]

Despawn removes matching objects created by RepoCommandConsole. Normal level content is outside its scope. To remove every enemy created by this mod, use /despawn enemy:all all. A numeric count is a maximum, so fewer removals can be a valid result.

[h2]5. Revive, heal, gather, or return the party[/h2]

Player commands always need a target: choose [b]all[/b], or type part of a player's name and accept the autocomplete entry. Entries include an actor number, such as "Bob Builder#2", to distinguish duplicate names. The host and dead characters are included. Up/Down reaches suggestions beyond the eight visible rows.

[code]/revive all
/heal all
/summon all
/truck all
[/code]

/revive revives eligible dead characters at their death heads; it requires an available death head and skips living characters. /heal fully heals living targets by default. To add a specific amount, accept a player's live selector and append a number:

[code]/heal "Bob Builder#2" 50
[/code]

/summon moves the selected characters or death heads to the command sender's position. /truck uses the truck safety spawn. To perform recovery in sequence:

[code]/chain all revive heal truck
[/code]

Each step finishes for the selected group before the next begins. A failed step stops the chain, so read the result before assuming later actions ran. Chains accept one to eight actions from kill, revive, heal, summon, and truck.

[h2]6. Let a friend use commands[/h2]

1. The host opens the console, types /grant , and accepts the friend's live name suggestion with [b]Tab[/b].
2. The host presses [b]Enter[/b]. The granted friend can now submit spawn, despawn, and player commands from their own console.
3. Run /permissions to inspect access.
4. The host can use /revoke  with the same selection flow to remove the friend's command access.

Grants belong to the current room and clear when the player leaves or the room/host changes. Only the host's local console can grant or revoke access. A grant allows the full command set, including actions affecting other players.

Unmodded friends can join but cannot open this console. Targets of /expression, /animationspeed, /pupils, or /falling also need [b]2.1.0 or newer[/b], even when they do not submit commands. They do not need a grant merely to receive an effect.

[h2]7. Explore the remaining player commands[/h2]

The player command set also includes /kill, /damage, /maxhealth, /knockback, /expression, /speak, /wings, /tumble, /flicker, /animationspeed, /pupils, /falling, and /resetpush.

For a visual example, select a player and try /wings <player> pink, then /wings <player> off. /maxhealth changes maximum health for the current runtime; it does not purchase a permanent upgrade, revive a character, or automatically fill the new maximum. Use the [url=https://github.com/jkieley/repo-live-control/blob/main/docs/commands.md#player-commands]full reference[/url] for each command's defaults and limits.

[h2]Troubleshooting[/h2]

- [b]F2 does nothing:[/b] confirm you used Start Modded, enabled the mod in the launched profile, installed both dependencies, and have not changed its toggle key in BepInEx configuration.
- [b]No canonical target matches:[/b] use Up/Down and Tab to accept a live catalog entry. Old screenshots and external name lists can differ from the installed catalog.
- [b]Permission denied:[/b] the host must grant access after you join the current room.
- [b]An effect is unsupported:[/b] confirm the host, command sender, and the target of an owner-applied effect are using 2.1.0 or newer.
- [b]A command partially completes:[/b] read the applied/skipped/failed result. Unavailable characters or failed placements can leave only part of a group affected.

[url=https://github.com/jkieley/repo-live-control/issues]Report a problem[/url] with the command, mod/game versions, multiplayer role, and relevant BepInEx log excerpt. [url=https://thunderstore.io/c/repo/p/Coollectors/RepoCommandConsole/]Download and screenshots[/url] are on Thunderstore.
